# A whole-file CRLF rewrite made a 12-line change land as 430 lines and
# reassigned blame for every line in two components. Line endings are LF in
# the repository, whatever the editing platform does locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which is not reliable with LF around
# multi-line constructs and labels. This is the Gradle wrapper: if it breaks,
# the Android build breaks with it. Gradle ships the same rule for the same
# reason.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Capacitor generates these, and `mobile/tools/android-assets/generate.mjs`
# hashes them ON DISK against `stock-res-checksums.txt` to tell a stock
# resource from one we customised. Normalising them would change those hashes
# on the next clean checkout and the asset gate would start calling stock files
# modified. Their byte identity belongs to upstream, not to our line-ending
# policy.
mobile/android/app/src/main/res/** -text
